      "text": "San José – Tortuguero National Park"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "9c6ebd267469089116190a5e05cc65d316151166324dcafc007002e6dbcd12dc",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-work-20261107162733338-r7kuchgsaf",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "Your journey starts early, at around 6:00 a.m. You leave San José by air-conditioned bus with a bilingual naturalist guide.\n\nThe route passes through Braulio Carrillo National Park, with views of dense tropical vegetation along the way. We stop for breakfast at the Selva Tropical restaurant, where you can see butterflies and a variety of tropical flowers in the garden.\n\nAfter breakfast, you continue to Caño Blanco, passing banana plantations. There you board a covered boat for the trip along the Tortuguero canals. Arrival is expected between 12:30 and 1:00 p.m.\n\nIn the afternoon, you visit the Caribbean Conservation Corporation’s Turtle Museum and then explore the colorful town of Tortuguero. Return to the lodge at about 5:30 p.m. Before dinner, you can relax by the pool or spend time at the bar. Dinner is served from 7:30 to 9:00 p.m., and the rest of the evening is free.\n\nOvernight at the hotel.  \n**Meals:** breakfast, lunch and dinner."
    },
